From: Escapement
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: register the CO5300 panel driver

co5300.c has been in the tree and working, but the build only ever picked it up
because the Kconfig entry and Makefile line had been added by hand to an
existing build tree. A clean build copies the driver in and compiles nothing:
`co5300` appears zero times in System.map, the panel never probes, and the only
symptom is a dark screen.

Found by the config check in build-kernel.sh, which is what it exists for -- the
kernel built fine, reported success, and had no display driver in it.

--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/Kconfig
@@ -1776,6 +1776,26 @@
 	  Configuration re: surface address, size, and format must be provided
 	  through device tree, or plain old platform data.
 
+config FB_CO5300
+	tristate "CO5300 AMOLED panel (T-Watch Ultra)"
+	depends on FB && SPI_MEM
+	select FB_CFB_FILLRECT
+	select FB_CFB_COPYAREA
+	select FB_CFB_IMAGEBLIT
+	help
+	  Framebuffer for the CO5300 AMOLED on LilyGo's T-Watch Ultra, driven as
+	  a spi-mem client.
+
+	  The panel speaks a protocol spi_transfer cannot express: an 8-bit
+	  command phase and a 24-bit address phase on one lane, then the pixel
+	  payload on four. It is write-only, so the only feedback is the
+	  tearing-effect pin, which pulses once per refresh while the controller
+	  scans.
+
+	  The cfb_* helpers draw into system memory and then hand the rectangle
+	  back through fb_ops, where this driver blits it to the panel. The
+	  sys_* variants would bypass that and the glass would never update.
+
 config FB_SSD1307
 	tristate "Solomon SSD1307 framebuffer support"
 	depends on FB && I2C
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/Makefile
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_OF)               += offb.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_SSD1307)	  += ssd1307fb.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_SIMPLE)           += simplefb.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_FB_CO5300)          += co5300.o
 
 # the test framebuffer is last
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_VIRTUAL)          += vfb.o
